# Live completed-solds API. Optional — Expo Go / `npx expo start` do not load eas.json
# env, so the same public Chamber comps.php URL is baked into the app when this is
# blank. Copy to `.env` only to override. After a pull, restart with:
#   npx expo start -c
# Query params sent: cardCode, language (EN|JP), type, grade, printNote, completed=true
# Quick (Get comps): sends months=6 so one call can cover Last 6 months.
# Last 6 months view groups those solds immediately — no second SoldComps call
#   when rows already arrived (avoids burning quota / wiping a good Quick result).
# If Quick was live n=0, Detailed may retry with mode=detailed&months=6.
# Same response shape. Extra rows welcome. Backend may still cap (often ≤20).
# Partial coverage is OK. Hostinger may need pagination later — UI does not block.
# Empty { solds: [], sourceMessage: "…quota…" } is an error, not fake live solds.
# Response: JSON array or { solds: [] } of completed solds. Each row needs:
#   id, cardCode, soldAt, channel (fixed|auction), completed=true,
#   priceAud, priceOriginal, currencyOriginal, type
#   sourceUrl (or listingUrl), optional sourceLabel, optional title,
#   optional imageUrl (or image_url / cardImageUrl / photoUrl) — shown after
#   Get comps even when solds are empty. Never invented.
# Prefer PriceCharting eBay solds, then eBay sold. AUD first; stamp FX on conversions.
# Public URL only. No secrets. The app never invents solds or sample prices.
#
# Default (baked in; also set in eas.json):
EXPO_PUBLIC_COMPS_API_URL=https://whitesmoke-woodpecker-609130.hostingersite.com/api/comps.php
